  "Question": "The ratio of Mary’s age to Alice’s age is \\(3 : 5.\\) Alice is \\(30\\) years old. How old is Mary?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(15\\)",
    "B": "\\(18\\)",
    "C": "\\(20\\)",
    "D": "\\(24\\)",
    "E": "\\(50\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Solution": "The ratio \\(3:5\\) means Mary's age is \\(\\frac35\\) of Alice's age. Since Alice is \\(30\\), Mary is\n\\[\n30\\cdot\\frac35=18\n\\]\nyears old. The answer is \\(\\boxed{18}\\), choice \\(\\mathrm{B}\\).",
